<title>UK: SBC Warburg repeats no comment on Dillon.</title>
<headline>SBC Warburg repeats no comment on Dillon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment bank SBC Warburg on Thursday declined to comment on a Wall Street Journal report that it would buy Dillon Read &amp; Co for about $600 million.</p>
<p>A Warburg spokesman said the bank was reiterating what a spokesman for its parent Swiss Bank Corp had said earlier in Switzerland. &quot;We have absolutely no comment,&quot; the bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal said that announcement of a deal, which would unite UK and U.S.-based investment banks each with strong lists of blue-chip clients, could come as early as today.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
